--  The run-time checks of the library build (ADASMB_CONTRACT_CHECKS=proved, the
--  default): GNATprove proves every contract of the SPARK core, so only the
--  preconditions, which guard the core against its trusted callers, are
--  checked. Postconditions and the other assertions, where the specifications
--  are used, are not run: one such as "the digest is SHA-256 of the message"
--  would compute the hash again on every call. Ghost code stays (Check),
--  because some preconditions call ghost functions; it runs only where a
--  precondition or a ghost statement uses it. The test build
--  (ADASMB_CONTRACT_CHECKS=all) checks everything.
pragma Assertion_Policy
  (Pre => Check,
   Pre'Class => Check,
   Post => Ignore,
   Post'Class => Ignore,
   Contract_Cases => Ignore,
   Assert => Ignore,
   Assert_And_Cut => Ignore,
   Assume => Ignore,
   Loop_Invariant => Ignore,
   Loop_Variant => Ignore,
   Ghost => Check);
